# docs/admin-guide/racoon-admin-guide.html's inline <svg class="doc-logo">
# (the racoon mascot illustration) has two <path> elements whose "d"
# attribute is long, tool-exported vector path data -- that data is the
# only form the illustration exists in, there is no separate, more
# "source" asset to include instead, and hand-wrapping generated path
# coordinates would risk introducing a transcription error for no
# benefit. All other over-length lines in this file and in
# doc/admin/split-dns.html were plain prose/markup and have been
# reflowed instead of overridden -- see the source-is-missing check's
# own "very-long-line-length-in-source-file" note.
ipsec-tools source: source-is-missing [docs/admin-guide/racoon-admin-guide.html]

# Bionic's lintian (2.5.81ubuntu1, frozen pre-release in Apr 2018) predates
# debhelper's debhelper-compat virtual package (added in debhelper 11.1.6,
# Aug 2018), so it can't parse the modern
# "Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 11)" compat declaration and falls
# back to assuming no compat is set at all. The build itself is correct --
# Bionic's debhelper is 11.1.6ubuntu2 and applies compat 11 properly, and
# lintian on Ubuntu Noble and beyond recognizes the syntax cleanly.
ipsec-tools source: debhelper-compat-file-is-missing
ipsec-tools source: package-uses-deprecated-debhelper-compat-version 1
ipsec-tools source: package-uses-debhelper-but-lacks-build-depends
ipsec-tools source: missing-build-dependency debhelper
